+# Existing application baseline (recorded BEFORE any Stage 1 change)
+
+Repository: `SbuKhoza/xploresoweto2`, base commit `14675c1` ("updated splash"). Stage 1 work happens on branch
+`stage1/firebase-transition`. This document is the reference for the final "same app, new infrastructure" comparison.
+
+## 1. Stack
+Expo 58 / React Native 0.88, React Navigation (native-stack + bottom-tabs), NativeWind, Firebase JS SDK v11
+(Auth + Firestore + Storage). No `expo-updates`/OTA, no Cloud Functions, no `firebase.json`, no rules files in the repo.
+Light theme only (`userInterfaceStyle: light`).
+
+## 2. Navigation (App.js)
+Root stack: `Splash` → `Authentication` (only when signed out) → `MainApp` (`MainGate`, only when signed in).
+Tabs: `Home`, `Xplore`, `Profile`, `Community`.
+* Xplore stack: XploreMain, Accommodation, Restaurants, Emergency, Recreation, Attraction, Transport, Business, Healthcare, PublicService, SowetoTownships.
+* Community stack: CommunityMain, Events, News, Eskom (loadshedding), **PoIst (Person-Of-Interest)**.
+
+## 3. Screens / features (all must remain)
+Splash; Authentication (login, sign-up, forgot-password, Google button); Enrollment gate (username, greeting, kasi);
+Home (hero, "The ultimate guide to Soweto" card, news/events feed, announcements, search over all collections, townships);
+Xplore menu + 9 category screens (list, search, detail modal, directions, call/WhatsApp actions);
+Business (list, detail, reviews, service request, hire); Restaurants + reservation form; Accommodation + reservation form;
+Emergency; Transport; Healthcare; Public services; Recreation; Attractions; Soweto Townships sheet;
+Events; News; Eskom loadshedding; Profile (photo upload, edit profile, change password, sign-out, clear cache);
+Community hub; offline mode (cache + indicators + clear-cache); Person-Of-Interest (posts, comments, images).
+
+## 4. Firebase dependencies (what the code actually does)
+### Authentication
+`createUserWithEmailAndPassword`, `signInWithEmailAndPassword` (login accepts an email **or a username**, resolved by a Firestore
+query on `users` BEFORE sign-in), `signOut`, `updateProfile`, `sendPasswordResetEmail`, `updatePassword` + re-auth, Google
+credential sign-in (placeholder client IDs, not functional). No email verification anywhere. Persistence: AsyncStorage
+(native) / browser local (web). A cached user object is also kept in AsyncStorage key `user` and used before Firebase confirms.
+
+### Firestore reads (client)
+| Collection | Read by |
+|---|---|
+| accommodations, attractions, recreation, healthcare, publicservice | `ExploreList` (unfiltered `getDocs`), Home search |
+| restaurants | `Restaurants.js:174`, Home search |
+| business | `Business.js:114`, Home search |
+| emergency, transport | `useOfflineData` (Emergency, Transport), Home search |
+| events, news | `useOfflineData` (Home, Events, News, Community) |
+| announcements | `useAnnouncements` (Home, Community) |
+| homescreen | `useHomeContent`, `useTownships`, enrollment kasi data |
+| xplore-menu | `Xplore.js:38` |
+| loadshedding | `Eskom.js:66` |
+| reviews | `Business.js:318,341` (`where businessId == …`) |
+| users | own doc: Home, Profile, Business, enrollment; **other users' docs**: PoIst; **username queries**: authService, enrollment |
+| Person-Of-Interest | `PoIst.js` (live `onSnapshot`), `Community.js:72` |
+
+### Firestore writes (client)
+`users` (authService:56 create; enrollment:114 merge; Profile:239,266 update), `reviews` (Business:351 `addDoc`),
+`userservices` (Business:371 `addDoc`, holds the requester's name/email), `loadshedding` (utils/seedLoadshedding.js, client seeding),
+`Person-Of-Interest` (create/update/delete/arrayUnion comments). Reservation forms store **nothing** and show a "confirmation email" alert.
+
+### Storage
+`profile-images/{uid}` (Profile.js:233), `person-of-interest/<random>` (PoIst.js:95). No deletes. Content images are URLs in documents.
+
+### Local storage (AsyncStorage)
+`user` (cached user), `collection_<name>[_filters]` and `doc_<name>_<id>` (offline cache), `enrollment:<uid>`, plus offline-mode metadata.
+
+## 5. Behaviour that matters for the transition
+* Content screens are CMS-driven; an empty collection shows each screen's existing empty state.
+* `Xplore.js` builds its tiles ONLY from `xplore-menu` documents (empty DB ⇒ no tiles).
+* `Eskom.js:73` seeds `loadshedding` from the client when empty.
+* No screen filters on `isActive`/`status` except news/events/announcements in Home and a few CMS-style lists.
+* Review/service-request eligibility is a client-side flag (`users.canReview`).
+
+## 6. Person-Of-Interest dependencies (documented before any change)
+`App.js:31,104` (import + `PoIst` route) → `Community.js:72` (read for a count) and `Community.js:120` (navigation card) →
+`components/personofinterest/PoIst.js` (reads `users`, writes `Person-Of-Interest`, uploads `person-of-interest/*`).
+**Proposed treatment:** hide behind a single feature flag (`utils/features.js`, default off): no route, no card, no read, no upload path,
+and no rules for the collection/folder. The component code is kept untouched for the later privacy/safeguarding review.
+
+## 7. Old Firebase project references
+Only `Firebase/config.native.js` and `Firebase/config.web.js` (project `the-steady-hotel`). No hard-coded bucket URLs elsewhere.
